    a: "Four signs our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check at every walk-in cooler diagnostic across LA commercial kitchens. (1) Compressor runs continuously but cabinet temperature drifts up — refrigerant charge low or compressor valves worn (year 7 to 10 typical wear curve). (2) Compressor short-cycles (runs 30 seconds, stops, restarts 60 seconds later) — stuck contactor, low refrigerant pressure triggering safety, or hard-start capacitor failure. (3) Audible knocking or grinding from the condenser unit — internal mechanical wear, often terminal. (4) Compressor body unusually hot to the touch (above 180°F casing) — internal failure imminent. We confirm with amp draw measurement against the data plate spec and head pressure on the manifold gauges. Compressor replacement on a walk-in scale runs $1,800 to $3,200 all-in including refrigerant recovery, evacuation, recharge, and EPA 608 documentation."
